###
PATCH /services/data/v61.0/composite/sobjects HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "allOrNone": false,
  "records": [
    {
      "attributes": { "type": "Account" },
      "Id": "0015g00000TrAd3AAB",
      "Rating": "Hot"
    },
    {
      "attributes": { "type": "Opportunity" },
      "Id": "0065g00000TrAd9AAB",
      "NextStep": "Send pricing"
    }
  ]
}
```

To fulfill the requirements—specifically that each order (Account upsert + Opportunity creation) succeeds or fails as an isolated atomic transaction without affecting other orders in the same API call—we use the **Composite Graph REST API** (`/services/data/vXX.X/composite/graph`).

Each graph in the payload represents an independent transactional unit of work identified by the order number (`graphId`). If any operation within a single graph fails, that entire graph is rolled back while the other graphs in the same request are still processed and committed.

```http
POST /services/data/v62.0/composite/graph HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "graphs": [
    {
      "graphId": "SO-1001",
      "compositeRequest": [
        {
          "method": "PATCH",
          "url": "/services/data/v62.0/sobjects/Account/Customer_Number__c/C-1001",
          "referenceId": "acct_1001",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Alder Creek Cafe"
          }
        },
        {
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "/services/data/v62.0/sobjects/Opportunity",
          "referenceId": "opp_1001",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Web order SO-1001",
            "StageName": "Closed Won",
            "CloseDate": "2026-09-26",
            "Amount": 1250,
            "AccountId": "@{acct_1001.id}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "graphId": "SO-1002",
      "compositeRequest": [
        {
          "method": "PATCH",
          "url": "/services/data/v62.0/sobjects/Account/Customer_Number__c/C-2002",
          "referenceId": "acct_1002",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Birch Lane Bakery"
          }
        },
        {
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "/services/data/v62.0/sobjects/Opportunity",
          "referenceId": "opp_1002",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Web order SO-1002",
            "StageName": "Closed Won",
            "CloseDate": "2026-09-26",
            "Amount": 980,
            "AccountId": "@{acct_1002.id}"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

To execute all three operations sequentially in a single transactional REST API call (where each record is saved to the database before the next subrequest runs, and the entire transaction rolls back if any subrequest fails), use the **Composite API** (`/services/data/vXX.X/composite`) with `"allOrNone": true`.

Note that the Composite Graph API is not suitable here because it groups unrelated records by depth and executes independent branches before dependent ones, which would cause `Service_Request__c` (depth 1, no lookup) to be inserted before `Asset` (depth 2, lookup to Account). The standard Composite resource executes subrequests strictly in the order they appear in `compositeRequest`.

```http
POST /services/data/v60.0/composite HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "allOrNone": true,
  "compositeRequest": [
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account",
      "referenceId": "newAccount",
      "body": {
        "Name": "Hollis Outdoor Supply"
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Asset",
      "referenceId": "newAsset",
      "body": {
        "Name": "Trailhead Kiosk 3000",
        "SerialNumber": "SN-88213",
        "AccountId": "@{newAccount.id}"
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Service_Request__c",
      "referenceId": "newRequest",
      "body": {
        "Subject__c": "Installation",
        "Serial_Number__c": "SN-88213"
      }
    }
  ]
}
