public with sharing class ErpCustomerSync implements System.Queueable, Database.AllowsCallouts {
    private static final Integer MAX_BATCH_SIZE = 200;
    private final List<CustomerPayload> payloads;

    public class CustomerPayload {
        public String salesforceId;
        public String name;
        public String country;

        public CustomerPayload(Account acc) {
            this.salesforceId = acc.Id;
            this.name = acc.Name;
            this.country = String.isBlank(acc.BillingCountry) ? null : acc.BillingCountry;
        }
    }

    public ErpCustomerSync(List<CustomerPayload> payloads) {
        this.payloads = payloads != null ? payloads : new List<CustomerPayload>();
    }

    public static void enqueueSync(List<Account> accounts) {
        if (accounts == null || accounts.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        List<CustomerPayload> payloads = new List<CustomerPayload>();
        for (Account acc : accounts) {
            payloads.add(new CustomerPayload(acc));
        }

        System.enqueueJob(new ErpCustomerSync(payloads));
    }

    public void execute(System.QueueableContext context) {
        if (this.payloads.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        List<CustomerPayload> chunk = new List<CustomerPayload>();
        for (Integer i = 0; i < this.payloads.size(); i++) {
            chunk.add(this.payloads[i]);
            if (chunk.size() == MAX_BATCH_SIZE || i == this.payloads.size() - 1) {
                sendCustomers(chunk);
                chunk.clear();
            }
        }
    }

    @TestVisible
    private static void sendCustomers(List<CustomerPayload> batch) {
        HttpRequest req = new HttpRequest();
        req.setEndpoint('callout:ERP/api/customers');
        req.setMethod('POST');
        req.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
        req.setBody(JSON.serialize(batch));

        new Http().send(req);
    }
}
```

### Explanation of Deviation

The prompt requested calling `EventBus.publish(event)` inside a `for` loop for each `Opportunity`. However, `EventBus.publish` counts toward the synchronous DML statement governor limit of **150 calls per transaction**. Because this method is invoked from an Opportunity trigger handler with batches of up to **200 opportunities**, calling `EventBus.publish` inside the loop would immediately throw an uncatchable `System.LimitException: Too many DML statements: 151` whenever a batch exceeds 150 records (or fewer, if other DML occurs in the same transaction).

Instead, the implementation builds a `List<Deal_Stage_Change__e>` inside the loop and makes a **single bulk call** to `EventBus.publish(List<SObject>)` outside the loop. This bulk overload:
1. Consumes only **1 DML statement** regardless of whether 1 or 200 opportunities are passed in.
2. Still returns a `List<Database.SaveResult>` in the exact same order as the input list, preserving the ability to inspect individual event failures by index without partial-batch rollback (`EventBus.publish` behaves like `Database.insert(..., false)` by default).

